    "note": "NOT ORIGINAL - the layer map read by tools/layers.ts (docs/architecture.md 'Layers'; the plan for the library split). A library may include itself and the libraries in 'allowed'. 'folders' are prefixes under the repository root; the longest prefix wins. 'strict' libraries have no upward include at all: not even the baseline may list one of theirs. The backends (render_pc, gpu_vulkan, audio_dsound, media_ffmpeg, input_dinput, fs_win32, net_winsock, script_qb) are included by app/ only: the editor and the front end reach the graphics backend through the engine's interfaces (render::Device, render::UiBackend; render_pc implements render::Device over render::Gpu, gpu_d3d9 is Direct3D 9's Gpu, GpuContext and UiBackend, gpu_vulkan Vulkan's), the engine reaches the sound output through audio::Device, the movie codec through media::Movie, DirectInput through its input::Source, the operating system's files through fs::Disk, Winsock's sockets through net::Transport and the QB script interpreter through script::Host. The editor's and the front end's 'api' lists the engine and game headers each may include (tools/layers.ts --api <library> prints what they include now); 'executables' says what an exe must do without (tools/cmake_layers.ts).",
